  **Content-Addressed Storage (Sec.2.6):**

  node_hash = SHA-256({
  semantic_hash: SHA-256({
  directive_id, lineage_id, deontic_type, evaluator,
  scope, severity_default, depends_on,
  priority, conflict_resolution, status, created_at
  }),
  presentation_hash: SHA-256({
  description, directive_revision, control_version
  })
  })
  edge_hash = SHA-256({
  source: directive_id,
  target: directive_id
  })
  snapshot_hash = SHA-256({
  node_hashes: sorted[],
  edge_hashes: sorted[],
  provenance: {
  engine_version, frozen_env_hash,
  directive_graph_version
  }
  })

  **Key Properties:**
  - compiled_at **excluded** from snapshot_hash
  - Incremental reuse via semantic_hash
  - Edge hashes independent of node content
end note

note right of finding_fsm_boundary
  **Finding FSM States (Sec.3.1):**

  Created -> Open -> Acknowledged -> Evidence Submitted
  |
  Pending Verification -> Verified -> Closed
  |
  Rejected
  ^
  Open -> Dismissed     Waived -> Closed

  **Terminal States:** Closed, Dismissed
  **Auto-Transitions:**
  - Evidence Submitted -> Pending Verification
  - Verified -> Closed
  - Waived -> Closed

  **Segregation of Duties (S-29, S-32, S-33):**
  - finding.waive: actor not in creator_provenance
  - finding.approve_remediation: actor not equal to evidence submitter
end note

